<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Louis V, Duke of Bavaria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1315–1361</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Louis the Brandenburger</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Louis V, called Louis the Brandenburger, was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/margrave-of-brandenburg">Margrave of Brandenburg</a> from 1323 to 1351 and later Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-bavaria">Upper Bavaria</a>. The eldest son of Emperor Louis IV of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-wittelsbach">House of Wittelsbach</a>, he received <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a> after the Ascanian line died out, but his rule was shaken by the impostor known as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/false-waldemar">False Waldemar</a>. His marriage to Margaret of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tyrol">Tyrol</a> in 1342 also brought him Tyrol.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/louis-v-duke-of-bavaria.jpg" alt="Louis V, Duke of Bavaria" width="270" height="580" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ernst Herter · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:LudwigI_Wittelsbach_Siegesallee.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
